subproblems.statement:
Let P, Q, j ∈ ℕ, let U ⊆ ℝ^P be open, V ⊆ ℝ^Q and A ⊆ U, and let f : ℝ^P → ℝ^Q be of class C^∞ with f⁻¹(K) ∩ A compact for every compact K ⊆ V. Then for every ω ∈ D^j(V) there are η ∈ D^j(U), ζ : ℝ^P → ℝ and an open set N ⊆ ℝ^P such that:
- A ⊆ N and 0 ≤ ζ ≤ 1;
- η(x) = ζ(x)·(f^#ω)(x) for all x, and η(x) = (f^#ω)(x) for all x ∈ N;
- tsupport η ⊆ f⁻¹(tsupport ω).
Here (f^#ω)(x) := ω(f(x)).compContinuousLinearMap (Df(x)).

For all P, Q, j ∈ ℕ, every continuous linear map L : ℝ^P → ℝ^Q and every j-covector α on ℝ^Q: |L^#α| ≤ ‖L‖^j·|α|. Here:
- L^#α := α.compContinuousLinearMap L, so (L^#α)(v₁, …, v_j) = α(Lv₁, …, Lv_j);
- |·| is covectorEuclideanNorm: for a j-covector β on ℝ^m, |β|² is the sum of β(e_{I(1)}, …, e_{I(j)})² over strictly increasing I : Fin j → Fin m (standard basis e);
- ‖L‖ is the operator norm for the Euclidean norms.
